# decimal_equal_compare — exact equality of two scaled decimals (README §27,
# R-067). Decimal is a scale-2 Int64 (raw = amount*100), so equality is an exact
# integer compare: 10.00 == 10.00 is decimal.equal(1000, 1000) -> true (1). No
# float epsilon — money compares exactly.
#
# Correctness observation: decimal.equal(1000, 1000) == true (1).
# Expected output: PASS lines + `---- 2 passed, 0 failed ----`

DecimalEqualCompare is project
DecimalEqualCompare module examplesDecimalEqualCompare
DecimalEqualCompare target console
DecimalEqualCompare entry main

examplesDecimalEqualCompare is module
examplesDecimalEqualCompare path examples.decimalEqualCompare
examplesDecimalEqualCompare exports main
examplesDecimalEqualCompare purpose "Compare two scaled decimals for exact equality"
examplesDecimalEqualCompare invariant "Equality is an exact integer compare"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

Decimal is alias
Decimal for Int64
Decimal purpose "Fixed-scale value: the raw Int64 is the amount * 100 (scale 2)"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Assert 10.00 == 10.00 exactly via decimal.equal"
main invariant "Writes the test harness summary"
main let priceA immutable Decimal 1000
main let priceB immutable Decimal 1000
main let harnessName immutable String "decimal_equal_compare"
main let trueValue immutable Int64 1
main let falseDecoy immutable Int64 0
main let noopName immutable String "decimal_equal_compare: real true (not the no-op false)"
main do compareEqual
main do writeResult
main do noopCheck
main do harnessReport
main return harnessSummaryCode

compareEqual is call
compareEqual in main
compareEqual invokes decimal.equal
compareEqual arg left Decimal priceA
compareEqual arg right Decimal priceB
compareEqual out areEqual Bool

writeResult is call
writeResult in main
writeResult invokes test.assertEqualInt64
writeResult arg name String harnessName
writeResult arg expected Int64 trueValue
writeResult arg actual Int64 areEqual

noopCheck is call
noopCheck in main
noopCheck invokes test.assertNotEqualInt64
noopCheck arg name String noopName
noopCheck arg expected Int64 falseDecoy
noopCheck arg actual Int64 areEqual

harnessReport is call
harnessReport in main
harnessReport invokes test.summary
harnessReport out harnessSummaryCode ExitCode
